(7786321, 1296125, 36065, '<td valign="top">
<b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b>
<br/>
<br/><b>My thoughts on the image:</b> I messed up on this whole challenge with my voting.  After seeing you ribbon, I really looked deeper into the golden ratio, and my understanding was way off.  I was expecting to see more flowing curvature in the image, so I did my voting on a wrong understanding of the challenge, rather than the quality of the overall images.  With that explained, embarrassingly enough, I was your 4 vote on this one.
<br/>
<br/><b>My ideas for improvement: </b> Now that I understand the golden ration, I love the photo.  The overlayed images really bring out every area of the picture nicely.
<br/>
<br/><b>Where I would have/did score this entry:</b> Well, aside from being the jackass that didn''t understand the challenge and handed out a low score, this SHOULD have been an 8 or 9 from me.  My apologies for bringing the scire down.  Overall, I probably didn''t drag it down too much, but still, I should have had a better understanding.  Thanks for sharing another awesome capture!
<br/>
<br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
<br/><b>Eric</b>
<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club

My thoughts on the image: I messed up on this whole challenge with my voting.  After seeing you ribbon, I really looked deeper into the golden ratio, and my understanding was way off.  I was expecting to see more flowing curvature in the image, so I did my voting on a wrong understanding of the challenge, rather than the quality of the overall images.  With that explained, embarrassingly enough, I was your 4 vote on this one.

My ideas for improvement:  Now that I understand the golden ration, I love the photo.  The overlayed images really bring out every area of the picture nicely.

Where I would have/did score this entry: Well, aside from being the jackass that didn''t understand the challenge and handed out a low score, this SHOULD have been an 8 or 9 from me.  My apologies for bringing the scire down.  Overall, I probably didn''t drag it down too much, but still, I should have had a better understanding.  Thanks for sharing another awesome capture!

Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,
Eric', '2025-08-07 09:15:44.000000', NULL, 0),
